# City bonds section on Economy → Loans (Figma band 11). Sells a ₡1,000 1-year bond through
# the section, checks its owed row and the refused state, then repays it with its Repay button.
# Costs the city a few cents of accrued interest at most; cleanup repays anything left.
name City bonds section: sell from the Loans tab, see the owed row, refused over the cap, repay
show-economy loans
bonds-section show
# Fixed finances (no debt, ₡1,000,000 a year), so the rate and the 3× cap (₡3,000,000) do not
# depend on the loaded city.
bond-finances 0 1,000,000
expect-visible FinanceOverhaulBondsSection
expect-hidden LoanDesc
bonds-term 1
bonds-amount 1,000
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsRate a year (3.00% +
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsSell Sell bond · receive ₡1,000
click FinanceOverhaulBondsSell
expect-log bonds: sold #
wait 0.6
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsOwedTitle Bonds you owe (
expect-visible FinanceOverhaulBondsRow-$bond
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsRepay-$bond Repay ₡1,000
capture bonds-sold
bonds-amount 3,500,000
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsHint Refused: the city would owe more than 3×
capture bonds-refused
bonds-amount 200,000,000
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsHint Refused: one bond can raise at most ₡100,000,000
click FinanceOverhaulBondsRepay-$bond
expect-log early from the Loans tab
cleanup:
redeem-new-bonds
bonds-section auto
close-dialog
close-economy
